+# Confirmed324 paired worker contract repair R2
+
+Source preparation only. No source acceptance, registration, lease, marker, worker process, runtime import, checkpoint deserialization, environment, training, evaluation, qualification, or checkpoint selection occurred. Three exploratory pairs remain descriptive, with no formal methods claim at n=3. Curriculum code and seeds were not used.
+
+## Files and authority
+
+- `worker_cli.py`: concrete future CLI; requires an externally hashed `parent_registered` registration, externally hashed exact parent source acceptance, parent-spent launch marker, inherited monotonic start, exact live lease, project interpreter, and existing empty cache. Validation mode uses stdlib only. Draft/unregistered status fails before runtime loading.
+- `runtime_adapter.py`: deferred real imports from the frozen runtime; exact loaded checkpoint/PPO function and teacher-method code checks; constructor bootstrap; accepted R5 private callbacks; raw rollout/PPO metrics; complete candidate saves. The historical runner is never executed. Its authenticated function definitions supply source identity and unchanged utility bodies.
+- `contracts.py`: full three-replica vector source pin, selected full vector/control equality, accepted reference/audit/registration pins, exactly two CPU/MPS digests, complete reference schema/study/replica/backend/Torch/checkpoint/receipt bindings, parent episode indices, all 64 SplitMix64 seed controls, exact five-range exclusions, accepted runtime member map and producing lineage.
+- `transition.py`, `driver_binding.py`, `attempt_claim.py`, `fingerprints.py`, `rng_reference.py`: byte-identical accepted R5 copies. No successor binding helper was needed. `source-manifest.json` is this output's authoritative content inventory, not parent acceptance. R5 authority remains the externally pinned parent manifest SHA `2b0caf00a5d5e765726d080fd5647211190e472d74ffb33b3466e477cb2906a9`; inherited R5 `source-hashes.json` is never used as authority.
+- `registration-template-replica-{1,2,3}-{A,B}.json`: inert templates. Placeholders and nonlaunchable status must be replaced by the parent, who pins the final source manifest and gates. No template grants authority.
+- `exact-diff.patch`, `diff-index.json`: exact comparison with R1 worker/builder, R5 test copies, and added files. Empty R5 implementation diffs are recorded explicitly.
+- `tests.log`, `fake-test-summary.json`, `receipt.json`, `interpreter.json`: fake controls, evidence limits, actual interpreter metadata. `tests-pass1.log` retains an initial test fixture failure; `tests-pass2.log` retains the prior passing iteration.
+
+## Adapter boundary and order
+
+1. Validate immutable input/source pins, full vector/reference and parent lineage, registration, source acceptance, marker, lease, interpreter and empty cache. Refuse existing run/attempt destinations.
+2. In a future authorized worker only, import pinned runtime, load the hash-pinned parent into a detached payload, validate complete-update schema/counters/identity/fingerprints, and check MPS. Loading a detached payload is not restoring a live learner.
+3. Run the frozen `seed_initialization` function body with `constructor_init_seed`; construct disposable model and Adam instances. This bootstrap necessarily precedes the R5 transition claim because R5 requires concrete bound instances. It does **not** restore accepted state. Initialization seeds may mutate generators before the transition claim; this is the explicit bootstrap boundary, not a claim-before-all-initialization guarantee. Source/launch acceptance must approve this boundary.
+4. Build R5 callbacks with authenticated source code, module dependencies, defaults and private globals. `restore_trusted` is a bound zero-argument closure. Never call it here.
+5. R5 validates source/reference/claim identity, atomically claims and fsyncs the fixed attempt path, marks its session consumed, then invokes that closure **once**. R5 verifies accepted model/Adam/six-raw-key RNG fingerprints, seeds Python, NumPy, CPU Torch, then MPS Torch; checks the **two** measured state digests; checks unchanged model/Adam; overrides LR after Adam restoration. A mutating failure consumes the attempt. No retry or alternate restore exists.
+6. Consume R5's actual evidence dictionary, without inventing a `transition_complete` status. Record bootstrap separately from R5's deferred-driver fields. Independently check raw six-key capture, CPU/MPS reference readbacks, scratch Python/NumPy seeded states, and live post-LR model/Adam fingerprints. Construct environment only after these checks and all 64 seed/exclusion controls.
+7. Run local updates 1–60, cumulative 373–432, phase 325–384. Constant LR is `3e-5`; linear is exactly `3e-5` at cumulative373 and `1e-5` at cumulative432. Preserve the pinned PPO controls, including `target_kl=.03`, 64 environments, rollout256, four epochs, minibatch512, raw diagnostics and CPU-shadow gradient diagnostics. No curriculum/control algorithm change.
+8. Preserve raw metrics, episode events, counters and mutable progress. Save complete immutable candidates at local12/24/36/48/60 (phase336/348/360/372/384); retain inherited counters and parent lineage, actual RNG, next episode indices, schedule/vector/exclusions and distinct resource/trajectory clocks. No partial-update candidate, automatic selection, promotion or evaluation occurs in this worker. Evaluation and selection remain separate parent-owned decisions.
+
+## Future CLI contract (not executed)
+
+The parent supplies these arguments to `worker_cli.py`: `--registration`, `--registration-sha256`, `--source-acceptance`, `--source-acceptance-sha256`, `--started`; optional `--validate-only` performs no runtime loading or mutation. Use the project `python/.venv/bin/python -B`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, and the parent's registered `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX`. Never run these templates as registrations.
+
+Source acceptance JSON must exactly contain `schema=paired_worker_parent_source_acceptance_v2`, `status=accepted_for_one_registered_worker`, the exact `registration_sha256`, `source_manifest_sha256`, and `run_id`. Parent launch marker must exactly contain `schema=paired_worker_parent_launch_marker_v2`, `run_id`, `registration_sha256`, and the inherited numeric `started`. The worker only reads parent lease/marker files and never clears, claims, repairs or rewrites them. Its separate R5 transition attempt path is new and durable.
+
+## Verification and remaining qualifications
+
+`run_fake_tests.py` installs an import blocker and empty `ModuleType` stand-ins for Torch/NumPy, then runs only owned tests with owned temporary directories and empty bytecode cache. The copied R5 real-Torch test was removed; R5 regression bodies remain unchanged. Fake arrays/models/Adam and stdlib copies exercise the actual R5 private restore/capture code and real adapter bootstrap; no accepted checkpoint was deserialized. Registration-only controls read/hash accepted files but construct only synthetic gate files under owned temporary paths. Fake candidate bytes are not accepted checkpoints.
+
+Remaining: independent parent source review/acceptance, final registrations for six runs, launcher/supervisor integration, hard watchdog/process-group cleanup and cancellation policy, resource calibration and caps approval, real accepted model/Adam/RNG restoration, actual loaded runtime/class/NumPy/MPS behavior, actual native all-slot readbacks, rollout/PPO/diagnostic compatibility, true candidate serialization and terminal audit. The accepted three references prove initial generator states only. Fake tests and static signature checks do not establish any real runtime result. Dependency versions are checked; Torch/NumPy package bytes are not pinned. Cooperative in-worker resource checks do not replace the parent watchdog. This Python in-process binding contract is not a sandbox against arbitrary code execution in the worker.
